n
is "x1 becomes/changes/converts/transforms into x2 under conditions x3",
which is too long for the card, and so was simplified to "x1 transforms int=
o
x2 under conditions x3". The jbofi'e {lo binxo} phrase is "any/some
become-r(s)", which after editing to get rid of the "any/some"s and various
punctuation became "become-rs". The definition of {lo binxo} for Smart.fm i=
s
"something that transforms", which not only corresponds to the definition
for {binxo}, but also, IMO, is easier to understand than the jbofi'e phrase=
.

